# Phase 7 — Match Current Pads Against the Terrain Map

### Step 7 — Now bring in the v6.2 Terrain workbook

Give Copilot:

1. Your cleaned Current Pad inventory.
2. `Defense_Tech_Opportunity_Intelligence_Terrain_Mapping_v6.2.xlsx`.

Tell it:

> Compare the Current Pad inventory against the Opportunities table in the terrain-mapping workbook.
>
> Look for credible adjacency based on:
>
> 1. Same program/platform
> 2. Same PMO/customer organization
> 3. Same prime/integrator
> 4. Same mission architecture
> 5. Same classification/trust boundary
> 6. Same platform family
> 7. Adjacent subsystem or site
> 8. Existing accreditation/integration that may reduce insertion risk
> 9. Existing product installation that could logically expand
>
> For every OpportunityID, classify the internal match as:
>
> * Confirmed Foothold
> * Potential Match
> * No Relevant Match
> * Needs Internal Follow-up
>
> For matches, identify:
>
> * OpportunityID
> * Current Pad
> * Evidence supporting the pad
> * Internal owner
> * Reference program/platform
> * Potential Target Pad
> * Proposed Current Pad → Next Pad path
> * Why the current position creates leverage
> * What must still be validated
>
> Do not infer that customer similarity alone proves adjacency.
> Do not assign a LilyPadScore yet.

This is where the **outside-in terrain map intersects the inside-out installed base.**

